    description: "The remaining owner of INV-nuzas's acceptance-property failure. Re-measure (self-analysis, dev 371adbe47c): 107 phantom hypergumbo_* external_symbol nodes, reached by calls (286) + module_attr_ref (106), ZERO imports edges. WI-noham (obj.method()/self.method()/@property/inherited) closed its own scope but only reduced this ~9 (116->107) — the residual is NOT receiver-typed methods. It is two dispatch:F3 shapes:\n\n(A) Cross-module IMPORTED-FUNCTION calls: `from x import fn; fn()` where fn is an in-tree module-level function -> the call dead-ends at python:<pkg.module>:0-0:fn:external_symbol instead of resolving to the real first-party function node. Samples: compute_cyclomatic_complexity, parse_tier_spec. (WI-gulot resolved the `f = g` ALIAS form; the direct `from x import fn; fn()` call form remains.)\n\n(B) module_attr_ref on module-level CONSTANTS/dicts + method calls on them: `mod.CONFIG_FILES_BY_LANG.items()`, `LANGUAGE_ALIASES.get(...)`, `KAFKA_STREAMS_CALLBACKS.values()` -> module_attr_ref edges (106) dead-end at phantom workspace externals.\n\nAcceptance property (INV-nuzas): no external_symbol canonical_name starts with a workspace prefix. Closing (A)+(B) drives the 107 -> 0 and closes INV-nuzas (its import facet F3/F4 already holds). Likely builds on the landed py.py scope-stack substrate (identity:F1/F4a) + the module_to_file_id map (F4) — resolve an imported-function callee and a module-attr-ref target to the in-tree first-party node the same way F4 resolved import edges. Re-measure INV-nuzas's phantom-external count after landing."  # eb2f
    fields: {}  # eb2f
