  message: "RE-SCOPE (design re-measure): this WI is a PARTIAL INV-nuzas close, not full. Corrected node accounting (self-analysis /tmp/hg-self.json): the 107 phantom hypergumbo_* external_symbol nodes = 55 calls-reached (11 CASE A imported-function + 44 CASE B receiver.method) + 52 module_attr_ref-reached (a SEPARATE _emit_module_attr_refs site, out of this WI's scope). WI-hotug covers CASE A (10 genuine re-exports; the 11th 'copy' is a WI-zigah misclassification) + CASE B (38 variable-receiver method calls; the other 6 = 5 scip_pb2 submodule-receiver + 1 TrackerApp class-receiver, deferred). So WI-hotug closes ~48-49 of 107.\n\nPR#1 / CASE B LANDED — dev e9afe8d556. Imported-const method call (CONST.items()) -> references edge to the in-tree kind=variable, guarded by _lookup_symbol_by_module(allow_ambiguous=False, INV-fahub) AND receiver_name not in _caller_locals (the review-caught scope-shadow guard: a param/local shadowing an imported constant must not mint a confidently-wrong resolved references edge). Behavioral: phantom hypergumbo_* externals 107 -> 68. Coherence 33->33, taint-neutral (references not in TAINT_CALL_EDGE_TYPES). Design + adversarial-review workflows (review NO_GO caught the scope-shadow false resolution + a missing kind-guard test).\n\nREMAINING for WI-hotug: PR#2 / CASE A — generalize the __init__.py-only re-export alias pass (py.py ~4859) to ALL modules (shadow guard: alias only when local_name not defined locally; DECOUPLE the re_exported modifier, keep it __init__.py-only for visibility.py/library-exports.yaml; bounded fixed-point cap 5 for N-hop chains). Closes ~10 more -> ~58.\n\nSIBLINGS (separate shapes, not WI-hotug): (1) module_attr_ref-reached phantoms (52 nodes, _emit_module_attr_refs site) — LARGEST remaining, filed separately below; (2) scip_pb2.* submodule-receiver -> generated-protobuf (5 nodes, needs module_to_file_id receiver resolution); (3) copy WI-zigah multi-segment-chain (1); (4) TrackerApp.__new__ class-receiver (1). Plus 2 CASE B review follow-ups: a same-name-collision test through the references path, and documenting the WI-gulot alias-variable-receiver behavior."  # bac9
